# Docker

## Multi-stage Chainguard pattern

Every Dockerfile uses a multi-stage build:
1. **Builder** stage on `cgr.dev/chainguard/<lang>:latest-dev` — has
   shell, package manager, build tools.
2. **Runtime** stage on `cgr.dev/chainguard/<lang>:latest` — distroless,
   nonroot, no shell.

Copy only what's needed from builder to runtime: the venv (Python),
the built `dist/` (Node), or the compiled binary (Go/Rust).

## Standard backend Dockerfile (Python + uv)

```dockerfile
# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7
FROM cgr.dev/chainguard/python:latest-dev AS builder
WORKDIR /app
ENV UV_LINK_MODE=copy \
    UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE=1 \
    UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/app/.venv

COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock ./
RUN uv sync --frozen --no-install-project --no-dev

COPY . .
RUN uv sync --frozen --no-dev

FROM cgr.dev/chainguard/python:latest
WORKDIR /app
ENV PATH="/app/.venv/bin:$PATH"
COPY --from=builder /app /app
EXPOSE 8000
ENTRYPOINT ["/app/.venv/bin/python", "-m", "uvicorn", "app.main:app", \
            "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000"]
```

## Standard frontend Dockerfile (Vue + pnpm + nginx)

```dockerfile
# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7
FROM cgr.dev/chainguard/node:latest-dev AS builder
WORKDIR /app
RUN npm install -g pnpm@9
COPY package.json pnpm-lock.yaml ./
RUN pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
COPY . .
RUN pnpm build

FROM cgr.dev/chainguard/nginx:latest
COPY --from=builder /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html
EXPOSE 8080
```

(Note: pnpm bootstrap via `npm install -g pnpm@9` is the cleanest path
on Chainguard's Node image. Pin the pnpm major version explicitly.)

## .dockerignore is mandatory

Every Dockerfile has a sibling `.dockerignore`. At minimum:
```
.git
.venv
node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
dist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
```

## docker-compose.yml

Local development only — never used to deploy. Includes:
- App services with `build:` referencing the Dockerfile
- Postgres with a named volume
- Healthchecks on every service
- `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` for ordering

## Forbidden

- `FROM python:3.x` or any non-Chainguard base
- `USER root` in production stage (only in builder, only if needed)
- `ADD <url>` — use multi-stage with verified downloads
- `latest` tags without an `@sha256:` pin in production deployments
- `RUN curl ... | sh` — see `02-supply-chain.mdc`
- `RUN apt-get update && apt-get install ...` (no apt in Chainguard;
  use `apk add` in `wolfi-base` if absolutely necessary)
- Building secrets into the image — use BuildKit `--mount=type=secret`
